<h1>SMS operating rules.</h1>
<p class="lede">Pass-vetting tells you the program is allowed to start. Operating rules keep it running. These four sets of rules cover what your team should do every day so the program stays compliant and customers stay opted in.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/support/messaging/checklist/">Readiness checklist</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/support/messaging/qa/">Pre-vetting QA</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Consent rules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Send only to subscribers who opted in to the specific brand and campaign type.</li>
		<li>Marketing messages require prior express written consent.</li>
		<li>Do not upload purchased, rented, scraped, shared, affiliate, or lead-gen lists.</li>
		<li>Keep SMS consent separate from email consent.</li>
		<li>Store consent evidence before sending and retain records for at least four years.</li>
		<li>Scrub marketing lists against the National Do Not Call Registry before first send and at regular intervals.</li>
		<li>Reconfirm consent when the campaign type changes materially.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Copy rules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Identify the brand in every message.</li>
		<li>Keep offers truthful and easy to understand.</li>
		<li>Use branded links — never public URL shorteners.</li>
		<li>Include STOP language in promotional campaigns, preferably every message.</li>
		<li>Avoid all disallowed or high-risk content.</li>
		<li>Match the registered use case and samples.</li>
		<li>Send only one opt-out confirmation message after STOP — no promotional content in that message.</li>
		<li>Do not send any further messages after the opt-out confirmation.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Frequency rules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Match the disclosed frequency.</li>
		<li>Avoid sudden spikes in volume.</li>
		<li>Cap daily / weekly sends by segment.</li>
		<li>Suppress recent purchasers or recent opt-outs from irrelevant campaigns.</li>
		<li>Marketing messages must not be sent before 8:00 AM or after 9:00 PM in the recipient's local time zone (TCPA quiet hours).</li>
		<li>Map recipient numbers to time zones and enforce quiet hours per number.</li>
		<li>For transactional messages outside quiet hours, still consider the recipient's time zone and expectations.</li>
		<li>Document send-window rules and enforce them in the scheduling or automation platform.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Support rules</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>HELP must return usable support contact information.</li>
		<li>Customer service must be able to confirm opt-in source and opt-out status.</li>
		<li>Support must never manually re-subscribe someone without a new opt-in event.</li>
		<li>Complaints should trigger review of the campaign, segment, copy, and opt-in source.</li>
	</ul>
</section>
